{
    "pr_body": "Motivation:\r\n\r\nDespite all the Connect reason codes was inventoried into the `MqttConnectReturnCode` the same wasn't done for the rest of MQTT messages. This would simplify the consumption of the messages, having a predetermined list of result codes as the one defined in the specification.\r\n\r\nModification:\r\n\r\nIntroduces a class which contains all the enums to cover Disconnet, PubSub etc reason codes.\r\n\r\nResult:\r\n\r\nFixes #13557 . \r\n\r\n",
    "original_commit_id": "64c898307de06a49f365093bb823bd4b7966c3d3",
    "merged": true,
    "pr_number": 13558,
    "pr_title": "[codec-mqtt] Add reason codes inventory",
    "lang": "java",
    "full_name": "netty/netty",
    "pr_comment": [
        "@chrisvest regarding \r\n> Where convenient, could we add some overloads that use the new enums?\r\n\r\nIn commit 75f337f98d8037310ebb1b840eab36e6dbfe6ee4 I've updated SubAck and UnsubAck payloads to use the newly introduced reason codes. Did you mean something like that?",
        "@andsel The Netty 5 mqtt module is [here](https://github.com/netty-contrib/codec-mqtt), if you're interested in porting the changes. Looks like it needs some love to make the build pass again.",
        "@chrisvest I try to move it to a green state. If and when I've something shareable, I'll put a PR :-) "
    ],
    "commit_id": "3a9ff0ddc2fdf77a688e231eef9f5f1c8210e65e",
