            ],
            "review_comment": [
                "This does not look correct. You initialize `VALUES` to have 28 elements, but the indexes are meant to be reason codes, which can extend to higher values because they are a sparse set. The highest index that we will assign here is 162:\r\n\r\n```\r\njshell> ((byte) 0xA2) & 0xFF\r\n$1 ==> 162\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo the LGTM warning is correct. The code needs to be fixed, instead of the warning silenced."
            ],
